  "text_md": "![](<304c1d231ac659ef6d0347a019cd838c2d725e2fad3a5b5f6dd76c578cb102ed_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\n## I1111111111111111 11111 111111111111111 lllll111111111111111 111111111111111111\n\nUS006503413B2\n\n# (12) United States Patent\n\n### (10) Patent No.: US 6,503,413 B2 (45) Date of Patent: Jan.7,2003\n\n#### Uchiyama et al.\n\n(54) STABLE, AQUEOUS COMPOSITIONS FOR TREATING SURFACES, ESPECIALLY FABRICS\n\n- 5,942,217 A 8/1999 Woo et al.\n\n- 5,955,093 A 9/1999 Woo et al.\n\n- 5,968,404 A 10/1999 Trinh et al.\n\n- 5,968,990 A 10/1999 Jon et al.\n\n- 5,997,759 A 12/1999 Trinh et al.\n- 6,001,343 A 12/1999 Trinh et al.\n\n\n- 6,033,679 A 3/2000 Woo et al.\n\n\n- 6,077,317 A 6/2000 Murphy\n\n\n- 6,100,233 A 8/2000 Sivik et al.\n\n\n- 6,106,738 A * 8/2000 Woo et al. .... ... ... ... 106/205.01 6,284,231 Bl * 9/2001 Trinh et al. ................ 424/76.1\n\n\n(75) Inventors: Hirotaka Uchiyama, Symmes Twp, OH (US); Janese Christine O'Brien Stickney, Wyoming, OH (US); Jonathan Robert Cetti, Fairfield, OH (US); Ricky Ah-Man Woo, Hamilton, OH (US); Dean Larry DuVal, Lebanon, OH (US); Gayle Marie Frankenbach, Cincinnati, OH (US)\n\n###### FOREIGN PATENT DOCUMENTS\n\nGB 805768 12/1958 JP 7109486 4/1995 WO WO 9807455 Al 2/1998 WO WO 9856429 Al 12/1998 WO WO 9856888 Al 12/1998 WO WO 9856890 Al 12/1998 WO WO 9910767 Al 3/1999 WO WO 9933669 Al 7/1999\n\n(73) Assignee: The Procter & Gamble Company,\n\nCincinnati, OH (US)\n\n( *) Notice: Subject to any disclaimer, the term of this patent is extended or adjusted under 35 U.S.C. 154(b) by Odays.\n\n- WO WO 9955814 Al 11/1999\n- WO WO 9955815 Al 11/1999\n\n\n- (21) Appl. No.: 09/783,509\n- (22) Filed:\n\n\n- WO WO 9955948 Al 11/1999\n- WO WO 9955949 Al 11/1999\n- WO WO 9955950 Al 11/1999\n- WO WO 9955951 Al 11/1999\n- WO WO 9955952 Al 11/1999\n- WO WO 9955953 Al 11/1999 WO WO 0008249 Al 2/2000 WO WO 0024851 A2 5/2000 WO WO 0024856 Al 5/2000 WO WO 0024858 Al 5/2000 WO WO 0030691 Al 6/2000 WO WO 0055292 Al 9/2000\n\n\n##### Feb. 14,2001 Prior Publication Data\n\n(65)\n\nUS 2002/0011584 Al Jan. 31, 2002\n\n##### Related U.S. Application Data\n\n(63)\n\nContinuation-in-part of application No. 09/634,379, filed on Aug. 9, 2000.\n\n###### (60)\n\nProvisional application No. 60/240,626, filed on Oct. 16, 2000, and provisional application No. 60/182,381, filed on Feb. 14, 2000.\n\n* cited by examiner Primary Examiner-Anthony J. Green\n\nInt. Cl.7 ............................................. D06M 15/643 U.S. Cl. .................... 252/8.91; 252/8.61; 424/76.1;\n\n- (51)\n- (52)\n\n\n(74) Attorney, Agent, or Firm-Jeffrey V. Bamber; Jason J. Camp\n\n424/76.2 Field of Search ............................... 252/8.61, 8.91; 424/76.1, 76.2\n\n(58)\n\n##### (57) ABSTRACT\n\nStable, aqueous compositions for treating surfaces, especially fabrics, comprise: a relatively low molecular weight polyalkyleneoxide polysiloxane surfactant; a buffering agent to maintain the pH of the composition in the range of from about 4 to about 10, preferably from about 5 to about 9.5, and more preferably from about 6 to about 9; and an aqueous carrier. The compositions can further comprise catoinic surfactants to further enhance the spreading and/or fabric penetration ability of the compositions. The compositions can further comprise a variety of other optional ingredients. Methods of treating surfaces include methods wherein the compositions are contacted with surfaces, especially fabrics, to reduce malodor impression on the surfaces and/or reduce the appearance of wrinkles in fabrics.\n\n##### References Cited\n\n(56)\n\nU.S. PATENT DOCUMENTS\n\n3,299,112 A *\n\nBailey ........................ 516/199 Bailey Rossmy et al. ............. 556/446 Rodriguez et al. Jacobson et al. Pings ...................... 424/70.12 Quincy, III et al. Quincy, III et al. Quincy, III et al. Desai et al. ................ 510/112 Mondin et al. ............. 510/101 Temperante Lucas et al. ................... 422/5 Dodd et al. ... .. ... ... ... ... ... 422/5\n\n1/1967\n\n- 3,359,212 A\n\n- 3,526,651 A *\n- 4,005,024 A\n\n4,661,268 A 5,482,703 A *\n\n- 5,500,254 A 5,525,415 A 5,540,984 A 5,654,262 A * 5,741,760 A * 5,804,625 A 5,858,335 A * 5,861,147 A *\n\n\n\n\n12/1967 9/1970 1/1977 4/1987 1/1996\n\n- 3/1996\n\n- 6/1996\n- 7/1996\n- 8/1997\n\n4/1998\n\n- 9/1998 1/1999 1/1999\n\n\n\n\n##### 29 Claims, No Drawings\n\n",
